### 1. Testing Zomato.com on iPhone 12, iPad, and Desktop

I opened Zomato.com in Google Chrome and used **F12 → Toggle Device Toolbar** to test the website in different screen sizes.

#### 3 UI/Layout Changes Observed

| View          | Observation                                                                                                                                 |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Desktop**   | The navigation bar has more space, and the search bar and other options are displayed horizontally.                                         |
| **iPad**      | The layout is still similar to desktop, but some elements have less spacing and are adjusted to fit the smaller screen.                     |
| **iPhone 12** | The layout becomes more compact. Text and images are resized, and some navigation options are simplified or moved to fit the mobile screen. |

**Other observations:**

1. Restaurant cards become smaller on mobile screens.
2. The number of items displayed in a row decreases as the screen size becomes smaller.
3. Spacing, font size, and navigation layout are adjusted to make the website easier to use on touch devices.

**Conclusion:** Zomato's website is responsive and changes its layout according to the screen size.

