### 2. Testing Flipkart Product Page at Different Screen Widths

I opened a Flipkart product page and slowly reduced the browser width from desktop size to mobile size.

| Approximate Screen Width   | Layout Change Observed                                                                                                       |
| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Above 1200px**           | Full desktop layout is displayed with large product images, product details, and navigation options.                         |
| **Around 1024px**          | Some spacing becomes smaller, but the page mostly remains in desktop/tablet layout.                                          |
| **Around 768px**           | Major layout changes start happening. Product information becomes more compact, and some sections may move below each other. |
| **Around 600px**           | The layout becomes more mobile-focused. Elements that were displayed side by side begin stacking vertically.                 |
| **Around 480px and below** | Full mobile-style layout appears. Text, buttons, and product images are resized to fit the smaller screen.                   |

**Major changes observed:**

* Navigation elements become more compact.
* Product details move from a side-by-side layout to a vertical layout.
* Buttons become easier to tap on smaller screens.
* Images resize according to the available screen width.

**Conclusion:** The main responsive breakpoints were approximately around **1024px, 768px, 600px, and 480px**. The exact breakpoint may vary depending on the current Flipkart page design.

